Ms. Padgett,<br />
<br />
The staff's deficiency letter in examination 2012-0126 of Rosslyn Padgett I=
nvestment Counsel (SEC File No. 801-65310) is enclosed. It describes six de=
ficiencies.<br />
<br />
Item 4 concerns best execution. The firm's policies require a periodic and =
systematic evaluation of the execution quality of the broker-dealers it use=
s. The staff found no such evaluation for 2010 or 2011. Ninety-one percent =
of the firm's equity order flow in the sample period went to a single intro=
ducing broker whose commission rate is above the rates the firm obtains els=
ewhere, and the firm's brokerage committee minutes record no discussion of =
execution quality in either year. The firm receives research and conference=
 access from that broker and treats the arrangement as within Section 28(e)=
 without having documented the required good faith determination.<br />
<br />
The other items concern the annual review, advisory agreement retention, tw=
o performance advertisements, the code of ethics reporting log, and the des=
cription of the firm's brokerage practices in Item 12 of Part 2A.<br />
<br />
Please respond in writing within thirty days on each item. Item 4 in partic=
ular should describe what the firm will do prospectively, not only what it =
believes about the past.<br />
